(7304016, 1139170, 179675, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kathyc:</b></div><hr/><i> The lack of focus on figure at right doesn''t help the image </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''ll be contrary and say it absolutely does help the image. Her lack of focus emphasizes distance and history between them.  <br/> <br/>A 5.2 on this is just simply tragic. Deserving of way higher than that.</td>', 'Originally posted by Kathyc: The lack of focus on figure at right doesn''t help the image   I''ll be contrary and say it absolutely does help the image. Her lack of focus emphasizes distance and history between them.   A 5.2 on this is just simply tragic. Deserving of way higher than that.', '2015-01-19 07:20:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7304017, 1138997, 163430, '<td valign="top">Did anyone noticed my blatant mistake in the math? I was writing RPM, but calculating Hz. It didn''t even ring any bells after the final result was 1/1250, which is way too short.<br/> <br/>Let''s fix it. 78 RPM = 1.3 Hz (rotations per second). That''s 3/4 seconds for a full record rotation. Given my initial estimate of 1/16th of a full circle recorded, the exposure time would be 3/64 seconds, which is approximately 1/22 seconds.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Did anyone noticed my blatant mistake in the math? I was writing RPM, but calculating Hz. It didn''t even ring any bells after the final result was 1/1250, which is way too short. Let''s fix it. 78 RPM = 1.3 Hz (rotations per second). That''s 3/4 seconds for a full record rotation. Given my initial estimate of 1/16th of a full circle recorded, the exposure time would be 3/64 seconds, which is approximately 1/22 seconds. ', '2015-01-19 07:23:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7304018, 1139055, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kroburg:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats on the TT.<br/>Sent you a PM re perspective. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Kees, I had a very quick attempt at the perspective correction and your suggested technique is great. I will spend a bit more time later this evening and see what I can come up with but here is a first stab<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1139868" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/135744/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1139868.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/135744/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1139868.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/135744/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1139868.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Originally posted by Kroburg: Congrats on the TT.Sent you a PM re perspective.   Thanks Kees, I had a very quick attempt at the perspective correction and your suggested technique is great. I will spend a bit more time later this evening and see what I can come up with but here is a first stab ', '2015-01-19 08:01:12.000000', NULL, 0),
