(7304134, 1138997, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by damjanev:</b></div><hr/><i>78 RPM = 1.3 Hz (rotations per second). That''s 3/4 seconds for a full record rotation. Given my initial estimate of 1/16th of a full circle recorded, the exposure time would be 3/64 seconds, which is approximately 1/22 seconds. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Which is pretty close to the stated time of 1/20. :-)<br/> <br/>I know someone with an Edison player -- I''ll have to keep it in mind for a future challenge ...</td>', 'Originally posted by damjanev:78 RPM = 1.3 Hz (rotations per second). That''s 3/4 seconds for a full record rotation. Given my initial estimate of 1/16th of a full circle recorded, the exposure time would be 3/64 seconds, which is approximately 1/22 seconds.  Which is pretty close to the stated time of 1/20. :-) I know someone with an Edison player -- I''ll have to keep it in mind for a future challenge ...', '2015-01-19 15:34:03.000000', NULL, 0),
